{
    "about": "The only components the Style sidebar may draw (owner, 2026-11-17; #8739): controls -- color pickers, menus, selects, buttons and the compact-mantine field controls they sit in. No pill, chip, badge, caption, sentence or warning. A component is approved only by adding it here. The lint rule graphty/eslint-rules/style-sidebar-controls.js refuses any other component from @mantine/* or @graphty/compact-mantine in the Style sidebar's files, and src/workspace/style/__tests__/SidebarControls.real-element.test.tsx walks the rendered sidebar and refuses any other element or any words outside them. A control's `dom` is its root as drawn (ControlLabel's also matches the plain `.ws-field-name` span the rows name their field with): everything inside it is the control's. A container holds controls; its own words may sit only inside `words`, and the rest of it is checked like the sidebar. `elsewhere` lists the components whose contents are not in the sidebar but beside it (a pop-over, a dialog, a menu's list), and `elsewhereProps` those whose props are (a tooltip's label): information may go there.",
